/* book exam traps: Taking fsc = 0.87 fy for Fe415. The curve reaches 361 N/mm² only at a strain of 0.0038; in the first example 361 N/mm² gives Asc = 211.9 mm² instead of 217.3 mm², 2.5 % unsafe. | Adding Asc without Ast2. The compression bars carry force only if extra tension steel balances them; without Ast2 the concrete block deepens past xu,max. | Writing Ast2 = Asc. That is true only if fsc = 0.87 fy. In the first example Ast2 = 211.9 mm² against Asc = 217.3 mm². | Designing with xu below xu,max when Mu > Mu,lim. The concrete block must be used fully (xu = xu,max) before steel is added; any other xu gives a different, uneconomic answer. | A large cover to the compression steel. With d′ = 150 mm in the first example, εsc = 0.0035 × 90/240 = 0.00131, still elastic, so fsc = 262.5 N/mm² and Asc = 34.43 × 10⁶/(262.5 × 350) = 374.8 mm². */
