/* book Worked example: Q: Floor beams of a hall are at 3.0 m centres, simply supported over an effective span of 7 m. Each has a web 300 mm wide, an effective depth of 550 mm and a monolithic slab 120 mm thick. It carries a factored moment of 400 kN·m. M25, Fe415. Find the effective flange width and the tension steel.
   1. bf = L0/6 + bw + 6 Df = 7000/6 + 300 + 6 × 120 = 1166.7 + 300 + 720 = 2186.7 mm. Spacing limit: 300 + 2700 = 3000 mm. Take bf = 2186 mm.
   2. Flange moment: Mf = 0.36 × 25 × 2186 × 120 × (550 − 0.42 × 120) = 2 360 880 × 499.6 = 1179.5 kN·m. Mu = 400 kN·m is far less, so the neutral axis is in the flange.
   3. Rectangle 2186 mm wide: 400 × 10⁶ = 0.36 × 25 × 2186 × xu × (550 − 0.42 xu), that is 8263 xu² − 10 820 700 xu + 400 × 10⁶ = 0, so xu = 38.1 mm (< 120 mm).
   4. Ast = 0.36 × 25 × 2186 × 38.1/(0.87 × 415) = 749 600/361.05 = 2074.6 mm².
   5. Provide 2 bars of 28 mm + 2 bars of 25 mm (1231.5 + 981.7 = 2213 mm²) in one layer: clear gaps (300 − 60 − 16 − 106)/3 = 39 mm, more than 28 mm.
   Answer: bf = 2186 mm; xu = 38.1 mm lies in the 120 mm slab; Ast = 2075 mm², provided as 2 of 28 mm + 2 of 25 mm (2213 mm²). */
