/* book Worked example 2: Q: A T-beam has bf = 1000 mm, Df = 100 mm, bw = 300 mm and d = 500 mm, with 6 bars of 25 mm in tension. M20, Fe415. Find its moment of resistance.
   1. Ast = 2945.2 mm². T = 0.87 × 415 × 2945.2 = 1063.4 kN. The flange alone at xu = Df gives 0.36 × 20 × 1000 × 100 = 720 kN < T, so the neutral axis is in the web.
   2. Try yf = Df: 0.36 × 20 × 300 × xu + 0.45 × 20 × 700 × 100 = 1 063 400, so 2160 xu = 433 400 and xu = 200.6 mm. But 3/7 × 200.6 = 86.0 mm < Df = 100 mm, so the slab is thicker than the flat zone and yf must be used.
   3. With yf = 0.15 xu + 65: 2160 xu + 6300 × (0.15 xu + 65) = 1 063 400, so 3105 xu = 653 900 and xu = 210.6 mm; yf = 0.15 × 210.6 + 65 = 96.6 mm (≤ 100 mm).
   4. xu,max = 0.48 × 500 = 240 mm, so xu < xu,max: under-reinforced.
   5. Cw = 2160 × 210.6 = 454.9 kN at an arm of 500 − 0.42 × 210.6 = 411.6 mm; Cf = 6300 × 96.6 = 608.5 kN at 500 − 96.6/2 = 451.7 mm. Check: 454.9 + 608.5 = 1063.4 kN = T.
   6. Mu = 454.9 × 0.4116 + 608.5 × 0.4517 = 187.2 + 274.9 = 462.1 kN·m.
   7. For comparison, Mu,lim,T at xu = 240 mm (Df/d = 0.2, so yf = Df) = 0.36 × 20 × 300 × 240 × 399.2 + 0.45 × 20 × 700 × 100 × 450 = 206.9 + 283.5 = 490.4 kN·m.
   Answer: Neutral axis in the web, xu = 210.6 mm, yf = 96.6 mm; Mu = 462.1 kN·m, below the T-beam limit of 490.4 kN·m. */
