/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - Divide the Annex G equation by b d² and both sides become stresses in N/mm²: Mu/bd² depends only on pt, fck and fy.
   - pt is the tension steel as a percentage of b d; Mu/bd² is in N/mm² with Mu in N·mm and b, d in mm.
   - The row above is computed from the formula; it is what the M25 table gives for Fe415.
   - For a doubly reinforced section the same idea gives pc = 100 (Mu/bd² − Mu,lim/bd²)/[fsc (1 − d′/d)] and pt = pt,lim + pc fsc/(0.87 fy), which is what Tables 45 to 56 list against Mu/bd².
*/
