/* book Worked example: Q: A beam 300 mm wide with d = 500 mm carries Mu = 150 kN·m. M25, Fe415. Find the steel with the design aid, then check it.
   1. Mu/bd² = 150 × 10⁶/(300 × 500²) = 2.00 N/mm², below 3.45 N/mm², so singly reinforced.
   2. The M25 table, Fe415 column, at 2.00 gives pt = 0.618 %.
   3. Ast = 0.618 × 300 × 500/100 = 926 mm². Provide 3 bars of 20 mm (942.5 mm²).
   4. Check: xu = 0.87 × 415 × 942.5/(0.36 × 25 × 300) = 126.3 mm; xu/d = 0.25 < 0.48. Mu = 0.87 × 415 × 942.5 × (500 − 0.42 × 126.3) = 152.6 kN·m ≥ 150 kN·m.
   Answer: pt = 0.618 %, Ast = 926 mm², 3 bars of 20 mm; the provided bars give 152.6 kN·m. */
