/* book Worked example 2: Q: The beam of the first doubly reinforced example (b = 250 mm, d = 500 mm, d′ = 50 mm, M25, Fe415, Mu = 250 kN·m) is designed with the doubly reinforced aid. Find pt and pc.
   1. Mu/bd² = 250 × 10⁶/(250 × 500²) = 4.00 N/mm², above 3.45 N/mm²; d′/d = 0.10.
   2. pc = 100 × (4.00 − 3.449)/[352.1 × (1 − 0.10)] = 0.174 %, so Asc = 0.174 × 250 × 500/100 = 217 mm².
   3. pt = 1.197 + 0.174 × 352.1/361.05 = 1.366 %, so Ast = 1.366 × 250 × 500/100 = 1708 mm², the same as the long calculation.
   Answer: pc = 0.174 % (217 mm²) and pt = 1.366 % (1708 mm²). */
